    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add an audio segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --kind <music|sound> \r\n                              Audio add kind: music / sound. Default music\r\n          --resource TEXT     Resource: local:///<abs_path> or vimo://<id>; bare filesystem\r\n                              paths are rejected\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 5s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --source-from TEXT  Resource source_from (remote music/sound id)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add background music from a local file over a 5s window\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio add --resource local:///x/y.mp3 --start 0s --duration 5s\r\n  # Add a sound effect from a resource id onto track 1\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio add --kind sound --resource vimo://123 --track 1\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Add an audio segment to the draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --kind <music|sound> \r\n                              Audio add kind: music / sound. Default music\r\n          --resource TEXT     Resource: local:///<abs_path> or vimo://<id>; bare filesystem\r\n                              paths are rejected\r\n          --track TEXT        Target track index. Unitless whole-number index.\r\n          --start <duration>  Timeline start, e.g. 0s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or\r\n                              min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Duration, e.g. 5s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --source-from TEXT  Resource source_from (remote music/sound id)\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Add background music from a local file over a 5s window\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio add --resource local:///x/y.mp3 --start 0s --duration 5s\r\n  # Add a sound effect from a resource id onto track 1\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft audio add --kind sound --resource vimo://123 --track 1\r\n",
